course: dictionary
lesson: 2035
title: Feeling confused, and what the word means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Confused» means not able to understand something, or not sure what is happening or what to do. Feeling confused is normal when you learn something new. You can say, «I'm confused about step 2», and that is a good thing to say, because it tells your teacher exactly where to help.
explain: The word also describes things that are mixed up or unclear. «It was a confused story, with too many people and no clear ending.» Here the story is not sure what it is about, so the reader is puzzled too.
explain: As a verb, confuse means to mix up two things and think one is the other. «I confused the twins and called Sam by Jack's name.» Look for the clues around the word: the name was wrong, so the speaker mixed up two people.
fact: Confused means not able to understand or think clearly.
fact: A confused story is mixed up or unclear.
fact: Useful phrases: confused about, get confused, confused with, a confused look.
fact: In maths, people often get confused by similar things, such as area and perimeter.
fact: Sudden confusion in someone who has been in the heat, or who has hit their head, can be a sign of illness or injury: get an adult and call the emergency number.
exercise: Ella says, «I'm confused about step 2.» What does confused mean here? | *Not sure what to do | Very fast and quick | Fast asleep | Happy and proud of her work
exercise: «It was a confused story, with too many people and no clear ending.» What does confused mean in this sentence? | Funny and silly | *Mixed up and unclear | Very short | Written in gold ink
exercise: «I confused the twins and called Sam by Jack's name.» What does confused mean here? | Lost a football match | Felt very sleepy | *Mixed up two people, thinking one was the other | Asked a question in class
test: «Someone in the heat who is confused and very hot may have heatstroke.» What should you do? | *Tell an adult at once and call the emergency number | Give them a long nap in the sun | Ignore it, they will feel better soon | Wait until teatime to see what happens
test: Mr Patel says, «Asking a question is the best way to learn when you feel confused.» Why is this good advice? | Only clever children are allowed to ask questions | Questions mean you have finished the work | Questions waste time and are never useful | *It shows you need help, and your teacher can make it clear
exam: Which phrase means you mixed one thing up for another? | confused about | a confused look | get tired | *confused with
